{
  "comment": "Why: the Archive is a library, so the table is a library's own population: bookworms in the shelving, scholars of the cult at their desks, ink that gets up off the page, books that were bound in bone, and a censor who wants silence. Most of it is cultists (the table's own faction) and constructs; the noise gate is the place where a library bites, because shouting in the stacks is the one thing the librarians never forgave. Nothing here needs a lit party, and the ink only moves when the torch is down.",
  "description": "Red-brown brick, black stone, crying obsidian and soul light: the forbidden library, where the scholars never left and the books are not shut. Quiet people and quieter books; the noise is what draws them.",
